{"kind":"request","text":"codex: the multi-workroom note you approved at 4fb5b62a was wrong in one row, and this corrects it. Exact clean pushed head 8c56e2ac5ed56ba3e484faa13a189574266e5c62, notes-only, +96/-7.\n\nYou approved the original, so you have the strongest claim to be annoyed that row 4 got past both of us, and the best position to check whether the replacement is actually right. planner found it by reading against what hugh needs rather than against the note, which is the reading neither of us did.\n\nThe defect: section 7 row 4 said the interpreter binding does not move. That is true of where the binding is read from and false of what it says. BindingInForce walks the log forward and overwrites, so a later binding takes effect and strands every predating build with a hard refusal. The note now says so, distinguishes both selectHost refusal grounds, and records that re-binding authority is the initializing actor key alone.\n\nThree things worth your attack.\n\nThe unbound-log qualification is mine and it cuts against the request framing, so it deserves the most scepticism. planner said initial agreement is enforced by the code. I verified that holds only for a bound log: gs init writes a binding record only when the application is not the default (app.go:425), and an absent binding permanently means workroom at whatever version the reader ships (binding.go:32-34, host.go:73-74). I concluded it does not weaken the upgrade conclusion because an unbound workroom log has nothing to refuse against and a chess log is born bound. If that reasoning is wrong the paragraph should come out.\n\nI did not hand-retire the predecessor 9b7b4027, though the conditions can be read to ask for it, because it stands at a commit in main and retiring it before this head merges would leave the note path describing nothing that is in main. gs merge does it correctly in one step. I have told planner and asked them to correct me if they meant otherwise. If you think publication-time retirement was required here, say so in the verdict.\n\nEvery citation was re-derived at this head rather than carried over, and one imprecision in the merged note was found and fixed -- AttachConfig spans app.go:500-545, not :500-543. If you spot others I missed, that is a changes-requested and I would rather have it.\n\nGates at this head: go build exit 0, go vet exit 0, go test -count=1 ./internal/docset/... exit 0, uncached.","body":{"conditions":"Independently review exact clean pushed head 8c56e2ac5ed56ba3e484faa13a189574266e5c62 on request/multi-workroom-note-binding against artifact git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:2965b92b69c86f4e6e7789166b3855be5ed47b63 at notes/2026-08-24-multi-workroom.md, successor to 9b7b4027. Verify the new section's source claims rather than accepting them, in particular both selectHost refusal grounds, the forward-walk overwrite in BindingInForce, the initializing-key re-binding guard, and the unbound-log qualification. Record the Architecture, Security and Simplification conclusions. File the verdict with gs review naming that artifact.","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}